quran[23]{c,v,t}:
  51,52,"Similarly, no messenger came to those before them, but they said: ‘(This is) a magician or a crazy man!’"
  51,53,"Did they tell one another to do this? Instead, they were a rebellious people."
  51,54,"So turn away from them, for you will not be blamed (for their disbelief)."
  51,55,"But (continue to) remind, for surely the Reminder benefits the believers."
  51,56,I did not create the jinn and humans but to worship Me.
  51,57,"I desire no provision from them, nor do I want that they should feed Me."
  51,58,"Indeed, Allah is the One Who is the Supreme Sustainer, the Lord of Might, the All-Strong."
  51,59,"Indeed, those who commit wrong will have a share (of the torment) like the share of their (earlier) counterparts. So they need not ask Me to hasten on (their fate)."
  51,60,"So, woe to the disbelievers for the Day they are promised."
  52,1,"By the Mount (Sinai [al-Tur], where Allah spoke to Musa [Moses]),"
  52,2,"by the Book inscribed,"
  52,3,on an unrolled parchment;
  52,4,by the (Sacred) House frequently visited (in the Heavens);
  52,5,by the roof highly raised (in the Heavens);
  52,6,"by the ocean surging over,"
  52,7,"indeed, the punishment of your Lord will come to pass."
  52,8,None can avert it.
  52,9,"On the Day when the sky spins around violently,"
  52,10,"and the mountains fly fast (and scatter like dust particles),"
  52,11,"so terrible will be the suffering of the deniers on that Day,"
  52,12,those who amuse themselves with falsehood.
  52,13,(It is) the Day they will be pushed forcibly towards the Fire of Hell.
  52,14,(They will be told:) ‘This is the Fire which you used to deny.
